WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.196 --> 00:00:25.785
Jack floundered in the deep end of the community pool while Coach Shin, Laura, and Mrs. Wilson took turns pushing his head under water.

2
00:00:25.786 --> 00:00:33.205
As Jack struggled for his life, Mrs. Wilson shouted at him, "Cup your hands, young man!"

3
00:00:33.206 --> 00:00:38.536
Jack sprang up, flung his arms out, and fought his attackers.

4
00:00:38.537 --> 00:00:45.610
Oh. There were no attackers. Jack was in bed, waking up from a terrible nightmare.

5
00:00:45.611 --> 00:00:50.761
He turned on his phone to check the time: it was only five o'clock in the morning.

6
00:00:50.762 --> 00:00:57.865
In the LED glow, he saw Luke with his thumb in his mouth, fast asleep under his superhero bedspread.

7
00:00:57.866 --> 00:01:03.434
He was so cute—during the rare times he wasn't talking or moving.

8
00:01:03.435 --> 00:01:12.515
Jack closed his eyes and tried hard to get back to sleep, but his mind was wide-awake, whirling with worries and thoughts.

9
00:01:12.516 --> 00:01:19.918
At five thirty Jack took his phone into the bathroom and called Noah. It was two hours later in Oklahoma.

10
00:01:19.919 --> 00:01:26.165
Noah would probably be awake; swim team practice always started early on summer mornings.

11
00:01:26.166 --> 00:01:32.745
After the third ring, Noah greeted him with a groggy, "Huh? Jack?"

12
00:01:32.746 --> 00:01:36.660
"Did I wake you up?" Jack asked, though he knew he had.

13
00:01:36.661 --> 00:01:42.913
Noah yawned in response.

14
00:01:42.914 --> 00:01:47.805
"Sorry," Jack said. "I really need a friend to talk to."

15
00:01:47.806 --> 00:01:51.160
"What's wrong?" Noah asked.

16
00:01:51.161 --> 00:01:54.013
The whole story came out in a rush.

17
00:01:54.014 --> 00:02:01.456
Jack told Noah about his family's tiny apartment and his humiliating first swim practice with the Sharks.

18
00:02:01.457 --> 00:02:06.050
Jack took a deep breath and blurted out more of his misery.

19
00:02:06.051 --> 00:02:12.134
"And then the pretty girl in my apartment building told my mother I hadn't been at practices.

20
00:02:12.135 --> 00:02:20.372
My parents made me clean the kitchen and apologize to my coach. And now he won't let me compete at the next meet. It stinks, right?"

21
00:02:20.373 --> 00:02:24.021
On the other end Noah stayed silent.

22
00:02:24.022 --> 00:02:28.945
"Noah? Are you still there?" Jack finally asked.

23
00:02:28.946 --> 00:02:36.613
"Yeah," Noah said. "Sorry you have to share a room with Luke. The kid is cute, but he can get annoying sometimes."

24
00:02:36.614 --> 00:02:42.017
"I know. Plus, my new swim team is a nightmare," Jack repeated.

25
00:02:42.018 --> 00:02:48.857
"This guy everyone calls Hulk is like Michael Phelps. He's got muscles on top of his muscles!"

26
00:02:48.858 --> 00:02:50.819
More silence.

27
00:02:50.820 --> 00:02:54.505
"Thanks for the sympathy," Jack said sarcastically.

28
00:02:54.506 --> 00:02:59.169
"You want my sympathy for not being the number one swimmer?" Noah asked.

29
00:02:59.170 --> 00:03:04.000
"I've never been the best on our team. You were always better.

30
00:03:04.001 --> 00:03:11.157
Jacob and Mark are better swimmers than I am too. Big deal." Now Noah was being sarcastic.

31
00:03:11.158 --> 00:03:19.666
"It's not just that," Jack mumbled. "I have to miss the first swim meet. It's a big one too, against the team's biggest rival."

32
00:03:19.667 --> 00:03:26.738
"You did ditch practice, Jack. You know that Coach Rayder wouldn't let you compete either if you missed several practices."

33
00:03:26.739 --> 00:03:28.888
Jack stayed silent this time.

34
00:03:28.889 --> 00:03:32.133
"I'm sorry things aren't going well for you," Noah said.

35
00:03:32.134 --> 00:03:35.974
"But there will be more swim meets this summer, right?"

36
00:03:35.975 --> 00:03:41.386
"Yeah," Jack muttered. "The season is just starting." He paused.

37
00:03:41.387 --> 00:03:45.075
"I guess I sound kind of whiny, huh?"

38
00:03:45.075 --> 00:03:47.466
More silence.

39
00:03:47.467 --> 00:03:52.725
"Okay, more than kind of whiny. I sound completely whiny," Jack said.

40
00:03:52.726 --> 00:03:58.765
"Yep," Noah said. "Stop feeling sorry for yourself, and just work on improving your swimming.

41
00:03:58.766 --> 00:04:02.354
I bet it'll all work out fine, even with that pretty girl."

42
00:04:02.355 --> 00:04:08.113
"Thanks, Noah," Jack said. "Speaking of girls, how are things with Kara?"

43
00:04:08.114 --> 00:04:16.258
Noah groaned. "We had one date—just one dumb date—and now she thinks I'm her boyfriend.

44
00:04:16.259 --> 00:04:21.915
She texts me a thousand times a day. If I don't text back right away, she calls me to ask what's wrong.

45
00:04:21.916 --> 00:04:24.942
And if I don't pick up her calls, she texts some more."

46
00:04:24.943 --> 00:04:29.590
"Ugh," Jack said. "That sounds awful."

47
00:04:29.591 --> 00:04:38.272
"It is awful," Noah said. "Sorry, but I have to go now. I have to get ready for swim practice. Good talking to you, Jack."

48
00:04:38.273 --> 00:04:42.761
"You too," Jack said. "Thanks for listening to all my complaints."

49
00:04:42.762 --> 00:04:46.106
"Good luck. And take my advice," Noah went on.

50
00:04:46.107 --> 00:04:51.836
"Don't give any girls your phone number, unless you want to spend all your time answering their texts and calls."

51
00:04:51.837 --> 00:05:01.234
Jack laughed. "That's probably really good advice," he said. Although he couldn't picture Laura texting him all the time.

52
00:05:01.235 --> 00:05:07.994
After they hung up, Jack thought about what Noah had said. Noah really did have some good points.

53
00:05:07.995 --> 00:05:14.828
Jack had to stop whining and start focusing on his swimming. Jack was glad he'd called Noah.

54
00:05:14.829 --> 00:05:21.217
A few minutes later, Jack got into his swimsuit. A swim would help him figure things out.

55
00:05:21.218 --> 00:05:26.468
He was hoping that there would be another swimmer there, but not crabby Mrs. Wilson.

56
00:05:26.469 --> 00:05:31.879
Jack left a note for his parents and hurried out of the apartment.

57
00:05:31.880 --> 00:05:39.123
But when he got to the pool, Mrs. Wilson was the only swimmer in the pool, floating on her back in the deep end.

58
00:05:39.124 --> 00:05:44.032
In her colorful bathing suit, her body resembled a huge beach ball.

59
00:05:44.033 --> 00:05:56.045
"Oh well," Jack thought. He waved at her half-heartedly before diving in and doing a few freestyle laps.

60
00:05:56.046 --> 00:06:03.451
When he stopped, Mrs. Wilson said, "Great job cupping your hands—if you were doing the breaststroke.

61
00:06:03.452 --> 00:06:08.352
You have to keep your hands cupped the whole time for the freestyle stroke.

62
00:06:08.353 --> 00:06:12.183
And you're not dropping your head enough to breathe properly.

63
00:06:12.184 --> 00:06:22.933
You should see my grandson do the butterfly. Little Tommy is like beauty in motion. The way he breathes—"

64
00:06:22.934 --> 00:06:29.987
"Grr!" Jack thought. He dived underwater and swam away.

65
00:06:29.988 --> 00:06:39.076
After a few strokes, just out of curiosity, he cupped his hands the way Mrs. Wilson had advised.

66
00:06:39.077 --> 00:06:44.399
Once again his stroke did seem smoother after he followed her advice.

67
00:06:44.400 --> 00:06:51.740
He tried lowering his head a bit. That seemed to make him faster.

68
00:06:51.741 --> 00:06:59.892
He swam to the shallow end of the pool. Maybe having Mrs. Wilson around wasn't so bad.

69
00:06:59.893 --> 00:07:03.705
He wondered how she knew so much about swimming techniques.

70
00:07:03.707 --> 00:07:09.147
He glanced at where she'd been floating on her back, but she was no longer there.

71
00:07:09.148 --> 00:07:13.208
He looked at the pool deck. She wasn't there either.

72
00:07:13.209 --> 00:07:25.298
Jack finally had the pool all to himself. He gazed happily across the glistening, peaceful water. "Ah," he said aloud. "Peace."

73
00:07:25.299 --> 00:07:38.050
Then he noticed a large, bright mass on the bottom of the pool. He stared at it. Not it—her—Mrs. Wilson. She wasn't moving.

74
00:07:38.051 --> 00:07:49.032
"Oh no!" Jack cried. Mrs. Wilson looked like she was unconscious . . . or dead!
